{"cuisine/cuisine-of-the-british-virgin-islands":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/cuisine-of-the-british-virgin-islands","n":"British Virgin Islands cuisine","c":"#94bd5c","crumb":[["The Americas","cuisines#the-americas"],["Cuisine"]],"sub":"National cuisine of British Virgin Is.","intro":[["Virgin Islander culture reflects the various peoples that have inhabited the present-day British Virgin Islands and U.S. Virgin Islands throughout history. Although the territories are politically separate, they maintain close cultural ties."],["Like much of the English-speaking Caribbean, the Virgin Islands culture is syncretic, deriving chiefly from West African, European and Indigenous Caribbean influences. Though the Danish controlled the present-day U.S. Virgin Islands for many years, the very dominant language has been the Virgin Islands Creole, a creole that is English-based, since the 19th century, and the islands remain much more receptive to English-language popular culture than any other. The Dutch, the French, and the Danish also contributed elements to the islands' culture, as have immigrants from the Arab world, India, and other Caribbean islands. The single largest influence on modern Virgin Islander culture, however, comes from the Africans enslaved to work in cane fields from the 17th to the mid-19th century. These African slaves brought with them traditions from across a wide swathe of Africa, including what is now Nigeria, Senegal, both Congos (the RotC and the DRC), Gambia, and Ghana."],["Virgin Islands culture continues to undergo creolization, the result of inter-Caribbean migration and cultural contact with other islands in the region, as well as the United States. Migration has altered the social landscape of both countries to the extent that in the British Virgin Islands, half of the population is of foreign (mostly Caribbean) origin and in the U.S. Virgin Islands, most native-born residents can trace their ancestry to other Caribbean islands."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"cuisine-of-the-british-virgin-islands"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cuisine_of_the_British_Virgin_Islands"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[]}],"cont":"Cuisine of the Americas"},"cuisine/indo-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/indo-cuisine","n":"Indo cuisine","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Asia","cuisines#asia"],["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine"]],"sub":"Diaspora cuisine in Indonesia","intro":[["Indo cuisine is a fusion cooking and cuisine tradition, mainly existing in Indonesia and the Netherlands, as well as Belgium, South Africa and Suriname. This cuisine characterized of fusion cuisine that consists of original Indonesian cuisine with Eurasian-influences—mainly Dutch, also Portuguese, Spanish, French and British—and vice versa. Nowaday, not only Indo people consume Indo cuisine, but also Indonesians and Dutch people."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"indo-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indo_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"Indo Dutch Kitchen Secrets: Stories and Favorite Family Recipes","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Jeff Keasberry","note":"Three generations of Indo (Dutch-Indonesian) family recipes; also published in Dutch as Indische keukengeheimen.","url":"","suggested":true}]},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Asian cuisine","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/1/11/Rijsttafel.jpg/500px-Rijsttafel.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Jan Willem van Wessel from Rotterdam, Netherlands","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rijsttafel.jpg"}},"cuisine/schleswig-holstein-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/schleswig-holstein-cuisine","n":"Schleswig-Holstein cuisine","c":"#cf5f87","crumb":[["Europe","cuisines#europe"],["German cuisine","cuisine/german-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in Germany","intro":[["The cuisine of Schleswig-Holstein forms part of the German cuisine in which the different influences of the regions Niedersachsen and Friesland and of Denmark are perceptible. The proximity to the sea and the harsh climate play a great role and determine which ingredients are available."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"schleswig-holstein-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Schleswig-Holstein_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["German cuisine","cuisine/german-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Part of","links":[["German cuisine","cuisine/german-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"European cuisine","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/2/25/Gr%C3%BCnkohl-Gericht-01_cropped.jpg/500px-Gr%C3%BCnkohl-Gericht-01_cropped.jpg","w":500,"h":433,"by":"Grünkohl-Gericht-01.jpg: horax zeigt hier derivative work: Hic et nunc (talk)","lic":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gr%C3%BCnkohl-Gericht-01_cropped.jpg"}},"cuisine/moldovan-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/moldovan-cuisine","n":"Moldovan cuisine","c":"#cf5f87","crumb":[["Europe","cuisines#europe"],["Romanian cuisine","cuisine/romanian-cuisine"]],"sub":"National cuisine of Moldova","intro":[["Moldovan cuisine is a style of cooking related to the people of Moldova. It consists mainly of ingredients such as various meats, potatoes, cabbage, and a variety of cereal grains. The local cuisine is very similar to Romanian, and also draws inspiration and elements from other cuisines in the region, including Greek, Ukrainian, and Russian, with an influence left by Ottoman cuisine."],["With the cuisine of Moldova being shared by another country, namely Romanian cuisine, there are similarities to these two cuisines of the two Romanian-speaking countries."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"moldovan-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moldovan_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["Romanian cuisine","cuisine/romanian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Dishes","count":8,"links":[["Blini","dish/blini"],["Borscht","dish/borscht"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Ostropel","dish/ostropel"],["Papanași","dish/papanasi"],["Sarmale","dish/sarmale"],["Scorcolga","dish/scorcolga"],["Stuffed peppers","dish/stuffed-peppers"]]},{"h":"Key ingredients","links":[["Cabbage","ingredient/cabbage"],["Ground meat","ingredient/ground-meat"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Milk","ingredient/milk"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Wheat","ingredient/wheat"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Beetroot","ingredient/beetroot"],["Beta vulgaris","ingredient/beta-vulgaris"],["Brassica oleracea","ingredient/brassica-oleracea"],["Carrot","ingredient/carrot"],["Potato","ingredient/potato"],["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"],["Lamb","ingredient/lamb"],["Rabbit meat","ingredient/rabbit-meat"],["Scallion","ingredient/scallion"],["Tomato sauce","ingredient/tomato-sauce"],["Cheese","ingredient/cheese"],["Grape leaves","ingredient/grape-leaves"],["Walnut","ingredient/walnut"],["Bell pepper","ingredient/bell-pepper"]],"note":"Most used across its dishes."},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Romanian cuisine","cuisine/romanian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"More from Moldova","count":1,"links":[["Gagauz cuisine","cuisine/gagauz-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"European cuisine","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/5/50/M%C4%83m%C4%83lig%C4%832020-02-12.jpg/500px-M%C4%83m%C4%83lig%C4%832020-02-12.jpg","w":500,"h":325,"by":"NicolaS961","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:M%C4%83m%C4%83lig%C4%832020-02-12.jpg"}},"ingredient/processed-meat":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/processed-meat","n":"Processed meat","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Processed meat is considered to be any meat that has been modified in order to either improve its taste or to extend its shelf life. Methods of meat processing include salting, curing, fermentation, smoking, and the addition of chemical preservatives. Processed meat is frequently made from pork or beef, but also poultry and others. It can contain meat by-products such as blood. Processed meat products include bacon, ham, sausages, salami, corned beef, jerky, hot dogs, lunch meat, canned meat, chicken nuggets, and meat-based sauces. Meat processing includes all the processes that change fresh meat, with the exception of simple mechanical processes such as cutting, grinding or mixing."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-processed-meat"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Processed_meat"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Thai cuisine","cuisine/thai-cuisine",[["American fried rice","dish/american-fried-rice"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Ketchup","ingredient/ketchup"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/c/c9/SelectionOfProcessedMeats.jpg/500px-SelectionOfProcessedMeats.jpg","w":500,"h":331,"by":"Raysonho @ Open Grid Scheduler / Grid Engine","lic":"CC0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SelectionOfProcessedMeats.jpg"}},"dish/arroz-carreteiro":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/arroz-carreteiro","n":"Arroz carreteiro","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Brazilian cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["Arroz carreteiro (\"wagoner's rice\", in Portuguese) or carreteiro rice is a dish from the Brazilian state of Rio Grande do Sul which has become popular throughout Brazil. It is made of a rice base to which shredded or cubed beef is added as well as carne-seca or carne-de-sol, paio, bacon or linguiça, a type of sausage. The dish is traditionally flavoured with garlic, onions, tomato and parsley. In the Central-West Region and the Northeast of Brazil, arroz carreteiro is also known as maria-isabel and it is prepared with carne-de-sol."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-arroz-carreteiro"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arroz_carreteiro"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Brazilian cuisine","cuisine/brazilian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":7,"links":[["Beef","ingredient/beef"],["Carne-seca","ingredient/carne-seca"],["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"],["Linguiça","ingredient/linguica"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Parsley","ingredient/parsley"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Olivia's Cuisine","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"oliviascuisine.com","note":"Brazilian-born Olivia Mesquita's blog, with a large section of Brazilian classics.","url":"https://oliviascuisine.com/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Easy and Delish","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"easyanddelish.com","note":"Brazilian recipe collection from a Brazilian-born home cook based in the US.","url":"https://www.easyanddelish.com/easy-brazilian-recipes/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Brazilian cuisine","links":[["Arabu","dish/arabu"],["Bauru (sandwich)","dish/bauru-sandwich"],["Beijinho","dish/beijinho"],["Beirute","dish/beirute"],["Bobó de camarão","dish/bobo-de-camarao"],["Bockwurst","dish/bockwurst"],["Bolo de fubá","dish/bolo-de-fuba"],["Brigadeiro","dish/brigadeiro"],["Canja de galinha","dish/canja-de-galinha"],["Coxinha","dish/coxinha"],["Feijoada","dish/feijoada"],["Maniçoba","dish/manicoba"],["Manuê","dish/manue"],["Marmelada de Santa Luzia","dish/marmelada-de-santa-luzia"],["Pão na chapa","dish/pao-na-chapa"],["Pie","dish/pie"],["Sobá","dish/soba"],["Xis (sandwich)","dish/xis-sandwich"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/7/77/Arroz_Carreteiro_1.jpg/500px-Arroz_Carreteiro_1.jpg","w":500,"h":334,"by":"Marcuskuhl","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arroz_Carreteiro_1.jpg"}},"ingredient/tomato-paste":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/tomato-paste","n":"Tomato paste","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 8 dishes across 10 cuisines","intro":[["Tomato paste is a thick paste made from tomatoes, which are cooked for several hours to reduce water content. The seeds and skins are then strained out and the liquid is cooked again to reduce to a thick, rich concentrate. Tomato paste is used to impart an intense tomato flavour in dishes such as pasta, soups and braised meat. It is used as an ingredient in many world cuisines."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-tomato-paste"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tomato_paste"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":10,"groups":[["Russian cuisine","cuisine/russian-cuisine",[["Beef Stroganoff","dish/beef-stroganoff"],["Goulash","dish/goulash"]]],["Turkish cuisine","cuisine/turkish-cuisine",[["Çiğ köfte","dish/cig-kofte"],["Kuru fasulye","dish/kuru-fasulye"]]],["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine",[["Barbecue sauce","dish/barbecue-sauce"]]],["French cuisine","cuisine/french-cuisine",[["Beef Stroganoff","dish/beef-stroganoff"]]],["Hungarian cuisine","cuisine/hungarian-cuisine",[["Goulash","dish/goulash"]]],["Iraqi cuisine","cuisine/iraqi-cuisine",[["Qeema Najafi","dish/qeema-najafi"]]],["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine",[["Cassoeula","dish/cassoeula"]]],["Kurdish cuisine","cuisine/kurdish-cuisine",[["Kısır","dish/k-s-r"]]],["New Caledonian cuisine","cuisine/new-caledonian-cuisine",[["Beef Stroganoff","dish/beef-stroganoff"]]],["Viennese cuisine","cuisine/viennese-cuisine",[["Goulash","dish/goulash"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Beef","ingredient/beef"],["Olive oil","ingredient/olive-oil"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Bulgur","ingredient/bulgur"],["Ketchup","ingredient/ketchup"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Tomato purée","ingredient/tomato-puree"],["Vinegar","ingredient/vinegar"],["Smetana","ingredient/smetana"],["Smetana (dairy product)","ingredient/smetana-dairy-product"],["Sour cream","ingredient/sour-cream"],["Cut of pork","ingredient/cut-of-pork"],["Pig's trotter","ingredient/pig-s-trotter"],["Pork","ingredient/pork"],["Pork ribs","ingredient/pork-ribs"],["Pork rind","ingredient/pork-rind"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/e/e8/Tomato_paste_on_spoon.jpg/500px-Tomato_paste_on_spoon.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"SKopp","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tomato_paste_on_spoon.jpg"}},"dish/bazin-bread":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/bazin-bread","n":"Bazin (bread)","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#e46a3f","intro":[["Bazin alternatively recognized as Bazeen, Bézine or Bazine  is an unleavened bread in the cuisine of Libya  prepared with barley, water and salt. Bazin is prepared by boiling barley flour or wheat flour in water and then beating it to create a dough using a magraf, which is a unique stick designed for this purpose. The dough may then be placed in a pan and allowed time to harden, after which it is baked or steamed. The salt contributes to the hardness of the bazin. Bazin may have a paste-like and hardened texture. It may also be prepared using whole wheat flour, olive oil, honey and/or pepper as ingredients."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-bazin-bread"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bazin_(bread)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Libyan cuisine","cuisine/libyan-cuisine"],["Tunisian cuisine","cuisine/tunisian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":2,"links":[["Barley","ingredient/barley"],["Wheat","ingredient/wheat"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Our Tunisian Table","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"ourtunisiantable.com","note":"Tunisian and Maghreb recipes such as lablebi and brik, written by Munya and Rim.","url":"https://ourtunisiantable.com","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Libyan cuisine","links":[["Mafrum","dish/mafrum"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/e/ee/Bazin.jpg/500px-Bazin.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Libiya11","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bazin.jpg"}},"ingredient/pita":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/pita","n":"Pita","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 4 dishes across 4 cuisines","intro":[["Pita or pitta (British English), also known as Greek bread (Greek: Ελληνικό ψωμί, romanized: Ellinikó psomí), Arabic bread, Arab bread (Arabic: خبز عربي, romanized: khubz ʿArabī), Syrian bread, Lebanese bread, and pocket bread, is a family of yeast-leavened round flatbreads baked from wheat flour, common in the Mediterranean, Middle East, and neighboring areas. It includes the widely known version with an interior pocket. In the United Kingdom, the term is used for pocket versions such as the Greek pita, used for barbecues as a souvlaki wrap. The Western name pita may sometimes be used to refer to various other types of flatbreads that have different names in their local languages, such as numerous styles of Arab khubz ('bread')."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-pita"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pita"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":4,"groups":[["Arab cuisine","cuisine/arab-cuisine",[["Shawarma","dish/shawarma"]]],["Brazilian cuisine","cuisine/brazilian-cuisine",[["Beirute","dish/beirute"]]],["Israeli cuisine","cuisine/israeli-cuisine",[["Sabich","dish/sabich"]]],["Turkish cuisine","cuisine/turkish-cuisine",[["İskender kebap","dish/iskender-kebap"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Lamb","ingredient/lamb"],["Lavash","ingredient/lavash"],["Laffa","ingredient/laffa"],["Cheese","ingredient/cheese"],["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Tomato sauce","ingredient/tomato-sauce"],["Yogurt","ingredient/yogurt"],["Amba","ingredient/amba"],["Amba (condiment)","ingredient/amba-condiment"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Eggplant","ingredient/eggplant"],["Hummus","ingredient/hummus"],["Israeli salad","ingredient/israeli-salad"],["Parsley","ingredient/parsley"],["Salad","ingredient/salad"],["Tahini","ingredient/tahini"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/3/32/Pita_Bread.jpg/500px-Pita_Bread.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Azure Dragon of the East","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pita_Bread.jpg"}},"ingredient/granulated-sugar":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/granulated-sugar","n":"Granulated sugar","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 4 dishes across 2 cuisines","intro":[["Sucrose (also called saccharose) is a disaccharide, a sugar composed of glucose and fructose subunits. It is produced naturally in plants and is the main constituent of white sugar. It has the molecular formula C12H22O11."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-granulated-sugar"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Granulated_sugar"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":2,"groups":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",[["Kue semprong","dish/kue-semprong"],["Sate klatak","dish/sate-klatak"],["Tinutuan","dish/tinutuan"]]],["Southern American cuisine","cuisine/cuisine-of-the-southern-united-states",[["Chess pie","dish/chess-pie"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Coconut milk","ingredient/coconut-milk"],["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Buttermilk","ingredient/buttermilk"],["Corn meal","ingredient/corn-meal"],["Shortcrust pastry","ingredient/shortcrust-pastry"],["Vanilla","ingredient/vanilla"],["Rice flour","ingredient/rice-flour"],["Black pepper","ingredient/black-pepper"],["Candlenut","ingredient/candlenut"],["Caraway seed","ingredient/caraway-seed"],["Cinnamon","ingredient/cinnamon"],["Clove","ingredient/clove"],["Galangal","ingredient/galangal"]]}]},"ingredient/mustard":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/mustard","n":"Mustard","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 2 dishes across 2 cuisines","intro":[["Mustard is a condiment made from the seeds of a mustard plant, which may be the white/yellow mustard (Sinapis alba), brown mustard (Brassica juncea), or black mustard (Rhamphospermum nigrum)."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-mustard"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mustard_(condiment)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":2,"groups":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine",[["Chicago-style hot dog","dish/chicago-style-hot-dog"]]],["Bangladeshi cuisine","cuisine/bangladeshi-cuisine",[["Shorshe ilish","dish/shorshe-ilish"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Mustard (condiment)","ingredient/mustard-condiment"],["Celery salt","ingredient/celery-salt"],["Chicago-style relish","ingredient/chicago-style-relish"],["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Hot dog","ingredient/hot-dog"],["Kosher dill pickle","ingredient/kosher-dill-pickle"],["Pickled cucumber","ingredient/pickled-cucumber"],["Poppy seed","ingredient/poppy-seed"],["Sport peppers","ingredient/sport-peppers"],["Tomato","ingredient/tomato"],["Vienna Beef","ingredient/vienna-beef"],["Vienna sausage","ingredient/vienna-sausage"],["White onion","ingredient/white-onion"],["Hilsa","ingredient/hilsa"],["Ilish","ingredient/ilish"],["Mustard oil","ingredient/mustard-oil"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/f/f4/Mustard.JPG/500px-Mustard.JPG","w":500,"h":331,"by":"fuji01","lic":"CC0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mustard.JPG"}},"dish/cha-trung":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/cha-trung","n":"Chả trứng","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Vietnamese cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Chả trứng, also chả trứng hấp (steamed) and chả trứng thịt (pork), is a Vietnamese steamed omelette, or egg meat loaf with pork. Trứng translates to egg, thịt translates to meat but is usually pork. It is usually served with hot rice, cucumber and chili sauce."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-cha-trung"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ch%E1%BA%A3_tr%E1%BB%A9ng"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Vietnamese cuisine","cuisine/vietnamese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":2,"links":[["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Pork","ingredient/pork"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Viet World Kitchen","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"vietworldkitchen.com","note":"Andrea Nguyen's blog on Vietnamese cooking, ingredients and technique.","url":"https://vietworldkitchen.com/blog/category/recipes-vietnamese","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Hungry Huy","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"hungryhuy.com","note":"Vietnamese-American Huy Vu's recipes for home-style Vietnamese dishes.","url":"https://www.hungryhuy.com/vietnamese/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Vietnamese cuisine","links":[["Bánh bao","dish/banh-bao"],["Bánh bột lọc","dish/banh-bot-loc"],["Bánh giầy","dish/banh-giay"],["Bánh tráng","dish/banh-trang"],["Chả rươi","dish/cha-ruoi"],["Chạo tôm","dish/chao-tom"],["Coconut candy","dish/coconut-candy"],["Cốm","dish/com"],["Khô cá lóc","dish/kho-ca-loc"],["Mắm nêm","dish/mam-nem"],["Nước chấm","dish/nuoc-cham"],["Ốc vú nàng","dish/oc-vu-nang"],["Shaking beef","dish/shaking-beef"],["Tương","dish/tuong"]]}]},"dish/garash-cake":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/garash-cake","n":"Garash cake","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Bulgarian cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Garash is a chocolate cake from Bulgarian cuisine. It was created by the Austro-Hungarian chef Kosta Garash in 1885 in Ruse, Bulgaria, during the time he managed the grand hotel “Islah Hane”, which was located next to the residence of the Bulgarian Knyaz Alexander of Battenberg. Royal figures, such as Carol I of Romania, Milan I of Serbia, and Oscar II of Sweden, were guests at the hotel. Kosta Garash created his famous \"Garash\" cake for such high-ranking receptions."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-garash-cake"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garash_cake"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Bulgarian cuisine","cuisine/bulgarian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Egg white","ingredient/egg-white"],["Powdered sugar","ingredient/powdered-sugar"],["Walnut","ingredient/walnut"]]},{"h":"More from Bulgarian cuisine","links":[["Banitsa","dish/banitsa"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["İmam bayıldı","dish/imam-bay-ld"],["Kolach (bread)","dish/kolach-bread"],["Kyopolou","dish/kyopolou"],["Lyutenitsa","dish/lyutenitsa"],["Patatnik","dish/patatnik"],["Pindjur","dish/pindjur"],["Sauerkraut","dish/sauerkraut"],["Stuffed peppers","dish/stuffed-peppers"],["Tarator","dish/tarator"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/1/1f/Garash.jpg","w":500,"h":338,"by":"Wiliamm at English Wikipedia","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Garash.jpg"}},"dish/goulash":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/goulash","n":"Goulash","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 3 cuisines","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Goulash is a meal made of meat and vegetables seasoned with paprika and other spices. Originating in Hungary, goulash is a common meal predominantly eaten in Central Europe but also in other parts of Europe. It is one of the national dishes of Hungary and a symbol of the country."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-goulash"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goulash"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Hungarian cuisine","cuisine/hungarian-cuisine"],["Russian cuisine","cuisine/russian-cuisine"],["Viennese cuisine","cuisine/viennese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":12,"links":[["Agaricus","ingredient/agaricus"],["Allspice","ingredient/allspice"],["Bay leaf","ingredient/bay-leaf"],["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Carrot","ingredient/carrot"],["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Olive oil","ingredient/olive-oil"],["Paprika","ingredient/paprika"],["Peppercorn","ingredient/peppercorn"],["Soy sauce","ingredient/soy-sauce"],["Tomato paste","ingredient/tomato-paste"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Zsuzsa Is in the Kitchen","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"zsuzsaisinthekitchen.blogspot.com","note":"Hungarian-born home cook's blog of traditional Hungarian recipes.","url":"https://zsuzsaisinthekitchen.blogspot.com/2010/01","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Olga's Flavor Factory","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"olgasflavorfactory.com","note":"Russian-born home cook Olga's blog, with a dedicated Russian recipes category.","url":"https://www.olgasflavorfactory.com/category/russianrecipes/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Plachutta: original recipes","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"plachutta.at","note":"Recipes from the Plachutta family's Viennese restaurants, known for Tafelspitz.","url":"https://www.plachutta.at/en/recipes/","suggested":true,"kind":"site"}]},{"h":"More from Hungarian cuisine","links":[["Arany galuska","dish/arany-galuska"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Chick